{"availability":"available","full":"Abidemialade/mylonite","name":"mylonite","description":"Open-source AI-layer security testing — probes your AI agent for weaknesses and writes a validated regression test for each one it finds, gating CI.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-09T02:21:36Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:41:23Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["agent-security","ai-security","llm-security","mcp","owasp","prompt-injection","pytest","python","red-teaming","security-testing"],"demo":"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.170Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.170Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.170Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.170Z","stars":2,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A safe model is not the same thing as a safe app. A top-tier model can shrug off every generic prompt-injection you throw at it and still hand an attacker a win — because the weakness is in how your app is wired, not in how the model behaves. Mylonite checks whether your app's own safeguards are what stop an attack, writes a test for every weakness it finds, and wires that test into CI so a future model upgrade cannot quietly remove the protection.","For teams shipping MCP or agentic apps who want CI-enforced regression coverage on the AI layer.","Point Mylonite at any MCP (Model Context Protocol) app. Mylonite's own agent reads your system prompt and tool descriptions and drives your tools itself — attacking the part an ordinary code scanner cannot see — finds weaknesses specific to your app, and turns each one into a pytest test that gates your CI. The API key you configure pays for that agent: the planner driving the attack, the customiser crafting payloads, and the judge scoring the result — not for a call your own app's agent made."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"27a42a5e5b84f9956fd1859c1cc5203caa29eb1c3b0602d91d1a553ba70dfe5b","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.348Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.348Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A safe model is not the same thing as a safe app. A top-tier model can shrug off every generic prompt-injection you throw at it and still hand an attacker a win — because the weakness is in how your app is wired, not in how the model behaves. Mylonite checks whether your app's own safeguards are what stop an attack, writes a test for every weakness it finds, and wires that test into CI so a future model upgrade cannot quietly remove the protection.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The API key you configure pays for that agent: the planner driving the attack, the customiser crafting payloads, and the judge scoring the result — not for a call your own app's agent made.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Scanning your own app needs a model: an API key for a hosted provider, or no key at all for one you host yourself (Ollama, vLLM, or a LiteLLM proxy — see self-hosted models). scan --scaffold and report never need a model at all, and demo replays recorded responses rather than calling one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"required","text":"Scanning your own app needs a model: an API key for a hosted provider, or no key at all for one you host yourself (Ollama, vLLM, or a LiteLLM proxy — see self-hosted models). scan --scaffold and report never need a model at all, and demo replays recorded responses rather than calling one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"--fast trades thoroughness for cost, and what it skips depends on the target: against your own app it skips the safeguard comparison itself, leaving a weaker check; against the bundled practice app the comparison is not optional, so it reduces the robustness checks instead.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"27a42a5e5b84f9956fd1859c1cc5203caa29eb1c3b0602d91d1a553ba70dfe5b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.349Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T14:41:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abidemialade/mylonite/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.350Z","hash":"27a42a5e5b84f9956fd1859c1cc5203caa29eb1c3b0602d91d1a553ba70dfe5b","originalBytes":22526,"storedBytes":22526,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["mylonite","docs","model","app","against","run","safeguard","scan","test","gate","own","every","finding","see","runs","demo","one","weakness","attack","practice","real","what","bundled","how","nothing","only","reference","full","key","rather","same","server","tool","which","api","check","command","comparison","install","mcp","bash","default","judge","kept","target","third-party","attacks","did","does","finds","limitations.md","needs","open","pip","python","results","step","still","two","verification","agent","any","before","cannot","control","could","each","evidence","extension","find","found","instead","license","models","published","pull","recall","request","result","scaffold","scope","them","tools","validate","version","where","write","writes","actually","agentdojo","authorize","build","built","carries","confirm","contributing.md","deliberately","env","failed","first","harness","measured","out","output","per","point","points","provider","pytest","read","reads","replays","report","security.md","stand-in","target.yaml","tells","there",